DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The definitions of the Apache License apply. In addition:

"WinTool" means the Work licensed under these terms, of which the Licensor is
the author.

"Modified Version" means a Derivative Work of WinTool, including a fork.

"Script" means a file that WinTool can read, configure or execute, and that
keeps its essential function when run without WinTool. A Script is NOT part of
WinTool and is NOT licensed under these terms, whoever wrote it.

"Script Source" means a catalogue from which WinTool can obtain Scripts.

"Corresponding Source" means the source code of a Modified Version in the form
preferred for making modifications to it, together with the scripts and
configuration needed to build it into the form distributed. It does not include
Scripts, Script Sources, or third-party components that are publicly available
under their own licenses, for which a reference and a version suffice.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. NO SALE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You may not Sell WinTool or any Modified Version.

"Sell" means doing any of the following for a fee or other consideration:

  (a) transferring a copy of WinTool or of a Modified Version;
  (b) granting access to it, including by download, hosting, streaming, or
      preinstallation on hardware;
  (c) granting a license to use it;
  (d) charging a subscription, rental, or any recurring fee for it or for
      continued access to it;
  (e) placing it behind a paywall, a paid registration, or a required donation;
  (f) making the price of any product, bundle, or package depend, in whole or in
      part, on the inclusion of WinTool;
  (g) charging for any feature of it, or for the removal of any limitation of it;
  (h) charging for access to a Script Source on which WinTool or a Modified
      Version depends in order to function.

You may not solicit or accept a donation, tip, or other payment in exchange for
access to WinTool or to a Modified Version, or as a condition of obtaining it.

CHARGING FOR SOMETHING ELSE IS NOT SELLING. The following are expressly
permitted, and nothing in this Section may be read to forbid them:

  (i)   using WinTool in the ordinary course of any activity, including the
        activity of a for-profit company of any size;
  (ii)  charging for installation, configuration, repair, maintenance, training,
        or support services, including services performed with the help of
        WinTool;
  (iii) charging for an IT service of which WinTool is a tool rather than the
        object;
  (iv)  distributing WinTool from a website, forum, or channel funded by
        advertising;
  (v)   monetising content that describes, reviews, or demonstrates WinTool,
        including sponsored content;
  (vi)  charging for a Script, which is not part of WinTool.

In each permitted case, WinTool itself must remain obtainable free of charge, and
the payment must correspond to goods or services other than WinTool.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. CORRESPONDING SOURCE ON DISTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

If You distribute a Modified Version in Object form to anyone, You must provide
its Corresponding Source to each recipient of that Object form, at no charge,
either together with the distribution or by a written offer, valid for three
years from the last distribution, to supply it on request.

You are NOT required to publish the Corresponding Source to the public, to the
Licensor, or to anyone who did not receive the Object form.

Using a Modified Version without distributing it to anyone outside the legal
entity that made it creates no obligation under this Section. Internal use is
not distribution.

Providing the Object form to a third party that is not part of that legal entity
is distribution, whatever the commercial relationship between them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. DISCLOSURE OF ADDED DATA COLLECTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WinTool as published by the Licensor contains no telemetry.

If a Modified Version You distribute collects, records, or transmits any
information about its users, their devices, or their use of it, beyond what a
feature the user has explicitly requested strictly requires, You must disclose
that clearly and conspicuously before installation, and identify what is
collected and to whom it is sent.

This Section states a licensing condition only. It does not replace any
obligation You may have under data protection law.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. IDENTITY OF THE PROJECT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

In addition to Section 6 of the Apache License:

You may not present a Modified Version as the official WinTool, nor use the name
"WinTool" or the project's visual identity in a way likely to suggest that a
Modified Version originates from or is endorsed by the Licensor.

A Modified Version You distribute must state clearly, where a user will see it,
that it is a modified and unofficial version, and must keep a reference to the
official repository.

Naming the origin factually — "based on WinTool" — is permitted and is not an
endorsement claim.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. SCRIPTS AND SCRIPT SOURCES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scripts and Script Sources are not part of WinTool and are not licensed under
these terms. Their authors choose their own terms freely, including commercial
ones.

WinTool reads Scripts, may recognise a format, may classify, configure and run
them. It adds no execution capability to a Script: a Script that does not work
without WinTool does not become functional by being loaded into it.

The Licensor does not control, review, endorse, or warrant Scripts or Script
Sources, including those WinTool marks as coming from the official Script
Source. Such a mark states provenance only. The Licensor is not liable for what
a Script does.

